From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:34:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] [M68k] Prevent folding of loads + stores when it would
 introduce new chain dependencies

Backport of upstream a6032d293c (llvm/llvm-project#175457) to Rust's
LLVM 22.1. A load folded into a memory-to-memory MOVE could tie two
call sequences together, and the scheduler then hit
'Assertion Best failed' or 'Couldn't find the register class'. rustc
crashed this way building compiler_builtins (rem_pio2_large, expf).
The two rmw.ll tests are regenerated for this tree.

Team 3
